IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `theft-nouns`
IMPORT `theft-s01-06-definition`
IMPORT `theft-s07-14-offences`

-- Theft Act 1968 ss 7 to 14: tests. Layer 1.
-- Every expected value was written by hand from the text of the section named
-- beside it, before the rule was run. Penalties are compared with penalty records
-- written out below ("expected ..."), not with the rules' own constants.
-- Yes/no fields of a fixture are FALSE unless the fixture's name says otherwise.

§ `Fixtures`

§§ `Expected penalties, written from the text`

GIVETH A `Penalty stated by the Act`
`expected seven years on indictment` MEANS `Penalty stated by the Act` WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
    `the imprisonment ceiling` IS (`imprisonment for a term not exceeding a number of years` 7)
    `the fine ceiling` IS `the section states no fine`
    `a fine and imprisonment may be imposed together` IS FALSE
GIVETH A `Penalty stated by the Act`
`expected life on indictment` MEANS `Penalty stated by the Act` WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
    `the imprisonment ceiling` IS `imprisonment for life`
    `the fine ceiling` IS `the section states no fine`
    `a fine and imprisonment may be imposed together` IS FALSE
GIVETH A `Penalty stated by the Act`
`expected fourteen years on indictment` MEANS `Penalty stated by the Act` WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
    `the imprisonment ceiling` IS (`imprisonment for a term not exceeding a number of years` 14)
    `the fine ceiling` IS `the section states no fine`
    `a fine and imprisonment may be imposed together` IS FALSE
GIVETH A `Penalty stated by the Act`
`expected ten years on indictment` MEANS `Penalty stated by the Act` WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
    `the imprisonment ceiling` IS (`imprisonment for a term not exceeding a number of years` 10)
    `the fine ceiling` IS `the section states no fine`
    `a fine and imprisonment may be imposed together` IS FALSE
GIVETH A `Penalty stated by the Act`
`expected five years on indictment` MEANS `Penalty stated by the Act` WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
    `the imprisonment ceiling` IS (`imprisonment for a term not exceeding a number of years` 5)
    `the fine ceiling` IS `the section states no fine`
    `a fine and imprisonment may be imposed together` IS FALSE
GIVETH A `Penalty stated by the Act`
`expected two years on indictment` MEANS `Penalty stated by the Act` WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
    `the imprisonment ceiling` IS (`imprisonment for a term not exceeding a number of years` 2)
    `the fine ceiling` IS `the section states no fine`
    `a fine and imprisonment may be imposed together` IS FALSE
GIVETH A `Penalty stated by the Act`
`expected summary six months or level 5 fine or both` MEANS `Penalty stated by the Act` WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
    `the imprisonment ceiling` IS (`imprisonment for a term not exceeding a number of months` 6)
    `the fine ceiling` IS (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5)
    `a fine and imprisonment may be imposed together` IS TRUE
GIVETH A `Penalty stated by the Act`
`expected summary level 3 fine only` MEANS `Penalty stated by the Act` WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
    `the imprisonment ceiling` IS `the section states no imprisonment`
    `the fine ceiling` IS (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3)
    `a fine and imprisonment may be imposed together` IS FALSE

§§ `A complete theft, used by the later fixtures`

`dis plain` MEANS `Dishonesty facts` WITH
    `believed in law he had the right to deprive the other of the property` IS FALSE
    `believed he would have the other's consent if the other knew` IS FALSE
    `believed the owner cannot be discovered by taking reasonable steps` IS FALSE
    `the property came to him as trustee or personal representative` IS FALSE
    `willing to pay for the property` IS FALSE
    `dishonest apart from the section 2(1) beliefs` IS TRUE
`dis honest` MEANS `Dishonesty facts` WITH
    `believed in law he had the right to deprive the other of the property` IS FALSE
    `believed he would have the other's consent if the other knew` IS FALSE
    `believed the owner cannot be discovered by taking reasonable steps` IS FALSE
    `the property came to him as trustee or personal representative` IS FALSE
    `willing to pay for the property` IS FALSE
    `dishonest apart from the section 2(1) beliefs` IS FALSE
`app assumed` MEANS `Appropriation facts` WITH
    `assumed the rights of an owner` IS TRUE
    `came by the property without stealing it` IS FALSE
    `later assumed a right to it by keeping or dealing with it as owner` IS FALSE
    `property or an interest in it was transferred, or purported to be, to him for value` IS FALSE
    `acted in good faith when it was transferred to him` IS FALSE
    `the rights assumed are rights he believed himself to be acquiring` IS FALSE
    `the only ground for calling it theft is a defect in the transferor's title` IS FALSE
`thing money` MEANS `Thing taken` WITH
    `kind of thing` IS `money`
    `in possession of the land` IS FALSE
    `authorised as trustee, personal representative, attorney or otherwise to sell or dispose of land belonging to another` IS FALSE
    `dealt with it in breach of the confidence reposed in him` IS FALSE
    `appropriated it by severing it, causing it to be severed, or after it had been severed` IS FALSE
    `in possession of the land under a tenancy` IS FALSE
    `remains in possession of the land after a tenancy ended, as statutory tenant or otherwise` IS FALSE
    `it is a fixture or structure let to be used with the land` IS FALSE
    `picked it for reward, or for sale or other commercial purpose` IS FALSE
    `it has been reduced into possession by or on behalf of another person and possession has not since been lost or abandoned` IS FALSE
    `another person is in course of reducing it into possession` IS FALSE
`bel possession` MEANS `Belonging facts` WITH
    `another had possession or control of it` IS TRUE
    `another had a proprietary right or interest in it` IS FALSE
    `every such interest of another is an equitable interest arising only from an agreement to transfer or grant an interest` IS FALSE
    `it was subject to a trust` IS FALSE
    `another had a right to enforce the trust` IS FALSE
    `he received it from or on account of another` IS FALSE
    `he was under an obligation to that other to retain and deal with it or its proceeds in a particular way` IS FALSE
    `he got it by another's mistake` IS FALSE
    `he was under an obligation to make restoration, in whole or in part, of it, its proceeds or its value` IS FALSE
    `it is property of a corporation sole, the office being vacant or not` IS FALSE
    `the other is the wife or husband of the person who appropriates it` IS FALSE
    `the other's interest in it is derived from the marriage` IS FALSE
`int lose` MEANS `Intention facts` WITH
    `meant the other permanently to lose the thing itself` IS TRUE
    `meant to treat the thing as his own to dispose of regardless of the other's rights` IS FALSE
    `the way he meant to treat it was a borrowing or lending` IS FALSE
    `the borrowing or lending was for a period and in circumstances making it equivalent to an outright taking or disposal` IS FALSE
    `had possession or control of the property, lawfully or not` IS FALSE
    `parted with the property under a condition as to its return which he may not be able to perform` IS FALSE
    `parted with it for purposes of his own` IS FALSE
    `parted with it without the other's authority` IS FALSE
    `meant to defeat the trust` IS FALSE
    `meant not to make restoration` IS FALSE
`theft all` MEANS `Theft facts` WITH
    `the dishonesty` IS `dis plain`
    `the appropriation` IS `app assumed`
    `the thing taken` IS `thing money`
    `the belonging` IS `bel possession`
    `the intention` IS `int lose`
    `with a view to gain or for his own benefit` IS FALSE
`theft but honest` MEANS `Theft facts` WITH
    `the dishonesty` IS `dis honest`
    `the appropriation` IS `app assumed`
    `the thing taken` IS `thing money`
    `the belonging` IS `bel possession`
    `the intention` IS `int lose`
    `with a view to gain or for his own benefit` IS FALSE


